    <bpmn:process id="W_W4869" name="W4869. Screening-Package Design — NBI/Police/Court, Employment, Education, Credit, Sanctions" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Role-package design (W4866); new role/source-country; source/quality issue
Frequency: Annual + on change
Volume: ~role-tier packages (5–7) × check-types
Owner: Screening Program Manager / Security (VS-159) / HR
Participants: Legal (VS-100.3), Finance (credit-check roles), Privacy (VS-91), Screening vendor
Source: workflow W4869 — Screening-Package Design — NBI/Police/Court, Employment, Education, Credit, Sanctions</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4869_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4869_Lane1" name="Screening Program Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4869_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4869_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4869_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4869_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4869_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4869_Start3" name="Role-package design (W4866); new role/source-country; source/quality issue">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4869_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4869_Task4" name="Design/maintain the check-type catalog: NBI clearance (national criminal)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Design/maintain the check-type catalog: NBI clearance (national criminal), police/barangay clearance (local), court-records check (regional trial courts), prior-employment verification (W3223-style reference checks), education/credential verification (links to PRC/TESDA W600/W558), credit check (finance/cash roles only, lawful), sanctions/PEP watchlist (links to VS-86), and drug test (VS-150)
Responsible (R): Screening Program Manager / Security / Legal / HR
Accountable (A): CHRO / Chief Compliance &amp; Security Officer
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4869_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4869_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4869_Task5" name="Map check-types to role-tiers (W4866): e.g., cashier = NBI + employment + drug…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Map check-types to role-tiers (W4866): e.g., cashier = NBI + employment + drug; finance = NBI + employment + credit + sanctions; security/CIT = enhanced NBI + court + sanctions; IT-admin = NBI + employment + sanctions; executive = full enhanced; ensuring proportionality and fairness
Responsible (R): Screening Program Manager / Security / Legal
Accountable (A): CHRO / Chief Compliance &amp; Security Officer
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4869_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4869_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4869_Task6" name="Maintain source-quality &amp; coverage: each check-type&#x27;s source (NBI, court…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Maintain source-quality &amp; coverage: each check-type&#x27;s source (NBI, court, school, employer, credit bureau), reliability, TAT, and gaps (e.g., court-records coverage varies by region); manage source-quality issues and alternative verification (links to W590 trade-pro verification)
Responsible (R): Screening Program Manager / Vendor / Legal
Accountable (A): CHRO / Chief Compliance &amp; Security Officer
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4869_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4869_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4869_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4869_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4869_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-731 (ensure controlled execution — Screening Program Strategy, Policy &amp; Governance (PA-167.1).) | - CTL-731: check-types mapped to role-tiers; proportionality enforced; source-quality monitored
Owner: Screening Program Manager / Security (VS-159) / HR</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4869_Assoc9" sourceRef="W4869_Annotation8" targetRef="W4869_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
