    <bpmn:process id="W_W4872" name="W4872. Screening Data Governance, Retention, DSAR &amp; Records Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Screen completion; retention-cycle; DSAR; audit; records-policy refresh
Frequency: Continuous + on retention/DSAR
Volume: All screening records (~thousands)
Owner: Screening Program Manager / Records (VS-88) / DPO (VS-91)
Participants: Legal (VS-100.3), HR, Internal Audit (VS-21)
Source: workflow W4872 — Screening Data Governance, Retention, DSAR &amp; Records Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4872_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4872_Lane1" name="Screening Program Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4872_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4872_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4872_Lane2" name="DPO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4872_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4872_Lane3" name="Records">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4872_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4872_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4872_Start5" name="Screen completion; retention-cycle; DSAR; audit; records-policy refresh">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4872_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4872_Task6" name="Govern screening-data retention: per RA 10173 data-minimization and the records…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Govern screening-data retention: per RA 10173 data-minimization and the records policy (VS-88), retain screening records only as long as necessary for the lawful purpose (employment/assignment duration + any statutory/defensive period), then securely dispose/sanitize; define retention by record-type
Responsible (R): Screening Program Manager / Records / DPO / Legal
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance / DPO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4872_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4872_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4872_Task7" name="Manage DSAR (links to VS-91): an individual&#x27;s access/rectification/erasure…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Manage DSAR (links to VS-91): an individual&#x27;s access/rectification/erasure request on their screening data, fulfilled within the statutory period, with legal/HR review where erasure conflicts with defensive-retention (negligent-hiring defense)
Responsible (R): DPO / Legal / HR / Screening Program Manager
Accountable (A): DPO
Duration: Per request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4872_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4872_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4872_Task8" name="Maintain records &amp; audit trail: secure storage, access controls (need-to-know)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Maintain records &amp; audit trail: secure storage, access controls (need-to-know), the chain-of-custody (W4870), and audit-ready production for regulator/internal audit (VS-21); reconcile to HRIS and legal-hold (VS-88); report records-health to governance (W4888)
Responsible (R): Records / Screening Program Manager / Internal Audit
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4872_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4872_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4872_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4872_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4872_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-131 (ensure lawful &amp; consented personnel vetting.) | - CTL-731: retention per RA 10173/records policy; DSAR honored; chain-of-custody &amp; audit-ready
Owner: Screening Program Manager / Records (VS-88) / DPO (VS-91)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
